  "Question": "On a map, a \\(12\\)-centimeter length represents \\(72\\) kilometers. How many kilometers does a \\(17\\)-centimeter length represent?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(6\\)",
    "B": "\\(102\\)",
    "C": "\\(204\\)",
    "D": "\\(864\\)",
    "E": "\\(1224\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "First find what one centimeter represents. Since \\(12\\) centimeters represents \\(72\\) kilometers, each centimeter represents \\(72\\div12=6\\) kilometers. Therefore \\(17\\) centimeters represents\n\\[\n17\\cdot6=\\boxed{102\\text{ kilometers}},\n\\]\nchoice \\(\\mathrm{B}\\).",
